<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albert II, Duke of Mecklenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1318">1318</a>–1379</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Albert II of Mecklenburg, Albert the Great</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Albert II was the ruler of Mecklenburg from 1329. In 1348 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iv">Emperor Charles IV</a> raised him and his brother John to the rank of dukes of the empire, and in 1352 the brothers divided their lands, John receiving Stargard. Albert extended his family's power around the Baltic, and in 1364 secured the Swedish crown for his son Albert. He died in 1379.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/albert-ii-duke-of-mecklenburg.jpg" alt="Albert II, Duke of Mecklenburg" width="284" height="500" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Theodor Fischer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Albert_II_of_Mecklenburg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
